__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# transient run output
data/run_log.txt
data/backfill_run.log

# Excel lock files
~$*.xlsx

# never commit anything credential-shaped
.env
*.env
secrets.*
*.pem
*.key

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# NOTE: data/raw/*.pdf, data/raw_reports.csv, data/listing_inventory.csv,
# data/listing_rowcount_highwater.json and output/* ARE committed on purpose.
#
#   - the PDFs are the primary evidence for the backfill
#   - the ledger is append-only history, and the future weekly Action reads it
#     for prior state and writes the updated version back
#   - the high-water mark must survive a fresh clone, or the shrink guard
#     silently re-baselines on the first run after cloning
#
# RULING 7, 2026-08-05 - the Architect REVERSED the earlier governance
# decision that would have gitignored data/raw/*.pdf. The PDFs STAY COMMITTED:
# they are the evidence any figure can be re-derived from, and 342 of them
# were already in history, so ignoring them would have stopped tracking new
# PDFs without removing the old ones - the worst of both. History was NOT
# rewritten.
#
# SIZE, measured 2026-08-05: 342 PDFs, 31.2 MB, mean 94 KB each. (An earlier
# note in this file said "~4 MB"; that was the pre-backfill figure of 39 PDFs
# and was carried forward without re-measuring. Corrected here.)
#
# REVISIT at 100 MB of PDFs. At 94 KB each that is ~1,094 reports: about 18
# more years at the current selection rate (~60/yr - weekly plus month-end),
# or about 4 years if the selection ever widened to every trading day. At that
# point move them to a release asset or LFS rather than dropping the evidence.
